  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C appears to exert its biological effects through a shared pathway involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which acts as a target of multiple entities, including Oblonganoside C, NCI-H1734, and Tyrosine-protein kinase Fer. These entities are all linked to SK-LU-1 via Ent-Gloeosteretriol, suggesting a potential mechanism where Oblonganoside C may influence SK-LU-1 through a common downstream target. The evidence indicates that Oblonganoside C may act as a modulator of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn affects SK-LU-1. The high scores in the paths suggest a consistent relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction between Oblonganoside C and Ent-Gloeosteretriol remains unclear. The presence of multiple targets for Ent-Gloeosteretriol implies that the pathway may be part of a broader network, and the integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Oblonganoside C could be a potential modulator of SK-LU-1 through this indirect route.",
